              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner Barnhart, the Coal Act requires the Commissioner to assign each beneficiary to a signatory coal operator before October\u202f1,\u202f1993, but the deadline is mandatory, not jurisdictional, and the Commissioner may continue assignments after that date if necessary."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3486416642b1c409be7fbb5a41ac20dadc5ce154ea173afaaa6581a7cf440d0a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3486416642b1-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 30
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "3486416642b1c409be7fbb5a41ac20dadc5ce154ea173afaaa6581a7cf440d0a",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3486416642b1-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondents argue that Congress\u2019s overriding purpose was to continue benefits, and that miners receive the same benefits whether they are assigned or not."
      }
    ],
